ahi: build the Bellatrix audio drivers on m68k

AHI's Raspberry Pi audio drivers are gated on two things: proto/dma.h, which
this target has, and $(filter arm aarch64,$(host_cpu)), which it does not
pass. So RPiHDMI has never been built here, and this machine has had no
audio path at all.

hdmiaudio, i2saudio and pwmaudio are our copies of RPiHDMI, RPiI2S and
RPiPWM, ported to m68k. For hdmiaudio and pwmaudio the `dsb sy` / `dmb sy`
it emitted around every register access are replaced with the compiler
barriers arch/m68k-emu68/include/asm/cpu.h already defines for the DMA and
USB paths; RPiI2S had no assembly at all and needed none. Under Emu68 there is no guest instruction that orders the host's
memory system -- the JIT and the host CPU do that -- and what is still needed
is to stop the compiler moving an access across the barrier.

Nothing else is changed. Every SoC table is kept, including the Pi 4 and Pi 5
ones this machine will not use: they cost nothing, a second board is a stated
direction for this port, and proto/openfirmware.h is present for
this target, so the device-tree probe they need compiles here too. Deleting
them would only widen the gap with the upstream driver and make its fixes
something to re-derive rather than apply.

The upstream RPi* drivers keep their arm/aarch64 filter untouched. They are
not ours and this target is not theirs.

--- a/workbench/devs/AHI/Drivers/Makefile.in
+++ b/workbench/devs/AHI/Drivers/Makefile.in
@@ -92,6 +92,20 @@
 SUBDIRS		+= RPiHDMI
 SUBDIRS		+= RPiI2S
 endif
+#
+# Bellatrix: the same hardware reached from m68k under Emu68.
+#
+# hdmiaudio is our copy of RPiHDMI, ported to m68k -- the ARM memory barriers
+# it emitted around every register access replaced by the compiler barriers
+# arch/m68k-emu68/include/asm/cpu.h defines, and the Pi 4 / Pi 5 device-tree
+# probe dropped along with the SoC tables it filled. The RPi* drivers above
+# stay arm/aarch64: they are not ours and this target is not in their filter.
+#
+ifneq ($(filter m68k,$(host_cpu)),)
+SUBDIRS		+= hdmiaudio
+SUBDIRS		+= i2saudio
+SUBDIRS		+= pwmaudio
+endif
 endif
 
